      "note": "Provisional machine alignment by Codex, independent Tibetan-first proposal. Sixty Verses on Reasoning is a work title, with its literal numeral member. ma rig is the established ignorance compound, not separately negated. rkyen is recast as the causal verb causes; can has no separate exponent in that conversion. gang phyir supplies causal For; the separate Why? is a rhetorical recast and is left unwrapped. mi 'thad is a negative phrase matched whole to wrong, not 'thad alone. The commentary's existence predicate grub pa is the English anaphoric does so, kept at phrase depth. rang/gi/ngo bos target essence of its own in English order; instrumental force lies outside the selected essence word. rnams is null only for plural morphology fused into worlds. tsam is omitted because restriction is distributed over none of them are anything more than, not cleanly isolated. rdzogs pa'i and quotation/description scaffolding without secure separate exponents are omitted. C05:235 repeats the quoted verse; C16:807 changes conceptions to projections, and ILL:1106 supplies a differently worded English rendering. These comparisons do not establish publication or ingestion independence."
